\h Genesis
\toc1 Genesis
\mt1 Genesis
\c 1
\s1 The Account of Creation
\p
\v 1 In the beginning God created the heavens and the earth.\f + \ft Or In the beginning when God created the heavens and the earth, . . . Or When God began to create the heavens and the earth, . . .\f*
\v 2 The earth was formless and empty, and darkness covered the deep waters. And the Spirit of God was hovering over the surface of the waters.
\p
\v 3 Then God said, “Let there be light,” and there was light.
\v 4 And God saw that the light was good. Then he separated the light from the darkness.
\v 5 God called the light “day” and the darkness “night.”
\p
And evening passed and morning came, marking the first day.
